This is version 0.4.1 plus one later change, the cliff guard
(vector_slam_maze/cliff_guard.py and its use in sdk_session.py). The version
string in pyproject.toml still reads 0.4.1.

This project is not affiliated with Anki or Digital Dream Labs; Vector is
their product. No third-party source files or assets are included.

In this published copy the robots' serial numbers, the robot's name and the
network addresses in defaults, documentation and tests were replaced by
made-up values (0dd1cafe, 0dd1beef, DEMO, 192.0.2.x). Set VECTOR_SERIAL or
pass --serial for your own robot. One test's optional check of a private
script now takes that script's path from CARTOGRAPHER_FRONTIERS_SCRIPT and
does nothing when it is unset.

README.md refers to findings and backlog entries kept in a private
workspace. The tests in this repository run offline, with no robot.
